# Entry Main. A reference input is a universal reference: `@: target Box` gives the place `target` its first value
# (a reference to Box), and that value is no requirement (L2 spec, reference places; the author 2026-11-23). So
# `Add\add(target := Other)` admits a Structure of another shape, and the body writes through the reference into the
# given Structure: `Other\z` 11. The first value Box stays as it was: `Box\q` 1 (step 21.7 K2).
# Norm: the book #structural-call; L2_spec, reference places: a two-argument `@: p Model` initially refers to Model
# itself; a full requirement belongs in the typed head `Model@`.
Box:
    int: q 1
end: Box
Other:
    int: z 1
    int: w 2
end: Other
Add:
    @: target Box
    add:
        target\z := target\z + 10
    end: add
end: Add
Main:
    Add\add(target := Other)
